## Hunt the Wumpus's claims: what the hunt can reach, each under the rooms,
## things and verbs that are load-bearing on the way. The test tree's
## manifest names this file; the story never imports it. The shared set is
## the winning hunt; a claim that needs less declares its own.

claims
  needs rooms: the Landing, the Echo Chamber, the Dripping Gallery, the Bone Hollow, the Bottomless Pit, the Sinkhole, the Bat Roost
  needs things: the coracle, the Wumpus
  needs verbs: enter, exit, look, steer, wait, set course for, shoot, heave to

  claim the Wumpus can be slain
    the story ends in victory

  claim the hunt can be lost
    the story ends in defeat

  claim the coracle reaches the Bottomless Pit
    the player is in the Bottomless Pit
    needs rooms: the Landing, the Bottomless Pit
    needs things: the coracle
    needs verbs: enter, set course for, wait

  claim the bats carry the coracle to the Bone Hollow
    the player is in the Bone Hollow
    needs rooms: the Landing, the Bat Roost, the Bone Hollow
    needs things: the coracle
    needs verbs: enter, set course for, wait, look
end claims
